WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.919
The phone page sends files between an iPhone and a Windows PC, over plain Wi-Fi.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.584
AirDrop needs Apple's own radio link, AWDL, and Windows can't run it.

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.847
So the phone page uses the Wi-Fi both devices already share.

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.929
On the PC, Your phone shows a QR code, and the iPhone's camera reads it.

5
00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:24.920
It holds the PC's address and a secret token, new every run.

6
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.957
Safari opens the page.

7
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.699
Pick five photos and tap Send.

8
00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:36.441
The upload is one request, and its order is the point: first the device, then the list of files, then the files.

9
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.976
The PC reads the list, then stops and asks, before it reads a single byte of the files.

10
00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:45.599
The phone has to wait.

11
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.587
Accept, and the photos stream across at Wi-Fi speed.

12
00:00:49.887 --> 00:00:51.999
They're saved together, or not at all.

13
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.684
What you agree to is what gets saved.

14
00:00:56.984 --> 00:01:01.464
If a file doesn't match the list, by name, size or count, nothing is kept.

15
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.215
This time, one photo.

16
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.768
Decline it, and the phone is told at once.

17
00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.180
Nothing is left behind on the PC.

18
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.056
Files can go the other way too.

19
00:01:14.356 --> 00:01:19.668
While the sheet is open, the PC offers files, and the phone saves them to its Files app.

20
00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.016
Links to an old offer stop working.

21
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.713
Two locks keep it safe: the secret token in the address, and the question on the PC.

22
00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:31.555
It's plain HTTP, so use it on a network you trust.

23
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.903
All of this was tested with a real iPhone, on iOS 27.

24
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.123
Not AirDrop. Just the Wi-Fi you already have.
